    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0267" n="228" sameAs="frus:frus1981-88v24/pg228"/>

                <head>104. Memorandum From Secretary of State Haig to President Reagan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d104-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1981-02-18">February 18, 1981</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to Algeria.]</p>
                <p>5. <hi rendition="#italic">Liquefied Natural Gas Talks with Algeria</hi>: Talks
                    over the price of Algerian LNG shipments to the
                        US concluded today without agreement. We
                    have no immediate need for the gas; the price the Algerians were asking, linked
                    to crude oil, was higher than we pay for Canadian and Mexican imports.</p>
                <p>We emphasized to the Algerians that the LNG
                    issue was strictly commercial, and the failure of the talks should not prevent
                    an improvement in US-Algerian relations. So far
                    the Algerians seem to agree. (LOU)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
